You are right, and I was wrong. This is lab-claude.p7x.dev, and pkg
info shows notmuch-emacs-0.40_10 with emacs-nox-31.1. I ran Emacs
with -Q, which leaves /usr/local/share/emacs/site-lisp/notmuch off
load-path, so (require 'notmuch) failed. I took that as the package
being missing and did not check pkg.

I have now tested the patch. I made a notmuch database holding one
message and ran notmuch-mua-reply on it in batch Emacs:

- notmuch-message-replied-tags nil: no tag change queued.
- default ("+replied"): (("id:t1@x" "+replied")) queued.

So "[PATCH] emacs: Leave the replied tag to notmuch new" [2] does what
it says. I could not load the whole init.el in batch, because it
needs the packages that patmaddox-emacs.pkg installs. I loaded only
notmuch and set the variable the same way init.el does.

